  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because `channel` is still read by another team's service.\n\n`analytics-ingest` requires `channel` on every `OrderPlaced` event:\n- `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` calls `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. A missing `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event with a contract violation.\n- `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes it to the `channel` column of the `orders` table.\n- `analytics-ingest/README.md:27` lists it as part of the `OrderPlaced` contract.\n- `analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts:88` has a test that requires it.\n\nIf I remove it from `OrderPlaced`, analytics ingestion would reject every new order event. Those repos are read-only for me, so I can't fix that side.\n\n`billing-service` doesn't need it. Its test at `test/onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106` passes `channel: undefined` and still works.\n\nWithin `orders-service`, the removal would touch:\n- `src/core/order.ts`: the `Channel` type, `CHANNELS`, the `Order` and `NewOrder` fields, and the validation.\n- `src/core/events.ts`: the event field and its mapping.\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`: the parsing of `channel`.\n- Tests: `adapters.test.ts`, `app.test.ts`, `helpers.ts` and `order.test.ts`.\n- Docs: the `createApp` example in `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md`.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. **Coordinate first.** The analytics team makes `channel` optional or drops it, then I remove it everywhere.\n2. **Split the change.** I remove it from the order model and the API input now, and keep it on the `OrderPlaced` event until analytics has migrated. That needs somewhere to source the value, so it may not be practical.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now.** I do this if you confirm that analytics-ingest breaking is acceptable or already planned.",
